{"name":"Mission Wildflower","hex":"#9e5566","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mission","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A set of tasks that fulfills a purpose or duty; an assignment set by an employer, or by oneself.","A important goal or purpose; an objective."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To send on a mission.","To do missionary work, proselytize."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mission"},{"term":"wildflower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wild (uncultivated) flowering plant.","A flower from such a plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wildflower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wildflower","blocks":[{"text":"A wildflower is a flower that grows in the wild, rather than being intentionally seeded or planted. The term implies that the plant is neither a hybrid nor a selected cultivar that is any different from the native plant, even if it is growing where it would not naturally be found. The term can refer to the whole plant, even when not in bloom, and not just the flower."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/07/DwSixspecies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wildflower","wikidata":"Q3585615"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Wildflowers_western_australia.jpg/500px-Wildflowers_western_australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Wildflowers_western_australia.jpg/500px-Wildflowers_western_australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wildflowers of Western Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWildflowers_western_australia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Grassland_Spring_Jewels%2C_Lake_Grapevine%2C_Texas_%28marcegottlie